.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd November 6, 2026
.Dt BSD3-USER-SESSION 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm bsd3-user-session
.Nd run an explicitly selected native user service graph
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar /absolute/services-directory root-service
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
starts Dinit in ordinary-user, container mode with only the selected service
directory. It creates a mode 0700 session directory beneath an owned, private
.Ev XDG_RUNTIME_DIR .
Root and mismatched real/effective user IDs are refused.
No system init service or machine shutdown facility is enabled.
.Pp
The process waits for Dinit and forwards interrupt, terminate and hangup as
a session shutdown. Dinit performs dependency-ordered stopping using each
service's explicit stop timeout. On FreeBSD the launcher additionally acquires
a process reaper and kills/reaps remaining descendants after Dinit exits.
This is scoped to this login, not all processes owned by the user.
Other operating systems have no additional orphan cleanup guarantee.
.Pp
Startup requires both the manager control socket and an acknowledged root
service start, including dependency readiness. The whole graph has a 120 second
startup deadline. Manager shutdown has a 30 second deadline; expiry is an error
and triggers forced manager/FreeBSD descendant cleanup. The manager's exit status
alone is insufficient evidence of a successful graph start.
.Pp
The experimental library
.Pa libbsd3-user-session.a
provides
.Fn bsd3_session_ready
and
.Fn bsd3_session_setenv .
Both return zero or a negative errno value.
Readiness writes one notification and closes the inherited pipe described by
.Ev BSD3_READY_FD .
Configure Dinit services with
.Li ready-notification = pipevar:BSD3_READY_FD .
The environment operation uses an owned socket in a private directory and
the configured dinitctl executable, with a five second response bound.
A NULL value removes a variable. Updates affect future services; existing
processes keep their environment. Arguments are passed directly, without a shell.
BSD3 control variables and DINIT_ variables cannot be changed by this API.
The pinned backend limits a name=value assignment to 1020 bytes; larger
updates fail with E2BIG instead of silently truncating the environment.
.Pp
The service directory is trusted executable configuration for the same user.
Every service must explicitly choose restart policy and finite startup/stop
timeouts. Session services must depend on the session-manager lifetime;
an independently started unbound service keeps the manager instance alive.
This program does not parse systemd units, provide sd_notify or
expose org.freedesktop.systemd1. These interfaces are experimental and do not
by themselves provide a GNOME 49 desktop.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width BSD3_SESSION_SOCKET
.It Ev XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Owned private runtime directory required for each login.
.It Ev BSD3_SESSION_SOCKET
Private per-login control socket set by the launcher.
.It Ev BSD3_READY_FD
Readiness pipe assigned by Dinit to an individual service.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dinit 8 ,
.Xr dinitctl 8 ,
.Xr dinit-service 5
